WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.640
Hey, everyone, we're going to start Kaleido Star!

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.410
When you watch Kaleido Star,
please keep your room brightly lit,

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.380
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.780
Well, well, well.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.620
What are your fun memories from
when you were small, everyone?

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.720
Going places with your mom and dad,
and doing things with them...

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.530
You were happy just to be together with them,

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.260
and those memories stay with you
no matter how much time goes by.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.630
They're wonderful treasures, aren't they?

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.960
Me, I'm here because that day happened.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:33.140
I won't forget.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.800
So I don't want you all to forget things, either!
I don't! I don't!

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:47.850
<i>Tattoo Kiss, the beginning is
red and black passions</i>

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:47.850
<i>Tattoo Kiss hajimari wa aka to kuro no Passion</i>

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:55.160
<i>Sometimes, we rely on our contrary hearts</i>

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:55.160
<i>Toki ni urahara na kokoro o tayori ni</i>

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.260
<i>Tattoo Kiss, the last resort is a
mission which changes the future</i>

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.260
<i>Tattoo Kiss kirifuda wa mirai o kaeru Mission</i>

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.920
<i>Tattoo Kiss, the last resort is a
mission which changes the future</i>

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.920
<i>Tattoo Kiss kirifuda wa mirai o kaeru Mission</i>

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.920
New Wings

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:09.870
<i>There is no place for ambiguous answers in love</i>

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:09.870
<i>Koi ni aimai na kotae wa iranai</i>

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:17.340
<i>Even while pretending not to see the
impossible reality, we bet</i>

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:17.340
<i>Arienai genjitsu minai furi shite mo Bet</i>

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:23.610
<i>Hard to obtain truth. Can you feel me now?</i>

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:23.610
<i>Egatai shinjitsu Can U feel me now?</i>

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:28.160
<i>Say what to myself who gets excited easily?</i>

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:28.160
<i>Nesshiyasui jibun ni Say What?</i>

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.520
<i>I'm confused, what to say</i>

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.520
<i>Tomadou iibun</i>

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:40.740
<i>Dreamin' the never-waking dream,
the falling fate</i>

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:40.740
<i>Dreamin' samenai yume ochiteku sadame</i>

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.500
<i>Don't stop lovin' can't stop lovin' you
Ya ya ya</i>

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.500
<i>Don't stop lovin' Can't stop lovin' U
Ya ya ya</i>

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:55.850
<i>I believe in you even if I lose everything for it</i>

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:55.850
<i>Believe in U hikikae ni subete ushinatte mo</i>

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:01.380
<i>Still lovin' can't stop lovin' you
No no no</i>

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:01.380
<i>Still lovin' can't stop loving' U
No no no</i>

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.990
<i>Tattoo Kiss</i>

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.990
<i>Tattoo Kiss</i>

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.670
Leon.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.430
Leon, are you listening?

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.430
Come on, Leon!

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.570
I'm listening.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.740
Say, make my training harsher.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:25.110
I want to perfect the Angel's Maneuver
before the Festival.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.320
This isn't the only year they'll hold the Festival.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.150
There's no need to rush.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:35.020
But it's already been more than
five years since we left Alain's...

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:38.430
That's okay, isn't it?
The time hasn't been wasted.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:43.530
After all, now all kinds of circus troupes
are inviting us to be guest performers,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.100
and we've even been nominated for the Circus
Festival, even if we are in the lowest seat.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.040
That's all because of you.
I'm just an extra bonus.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:57.780
To make up for my deficiencies, you're always
training yourself without a break.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.750
I want to work harder too!

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.710
This is just the habit I've had since
I was a kid, that's all.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.090
Never mind. I'll make my training harsher myself.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.030
Hey!

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.790
I'll perform the Angel's Maneuver
at the Circus Festival.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:13.860
Perfectly!

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.860
Sophie!

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.000
Okay, I get it.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.860
We'll toughen up the practice menu
for the Festival.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.670
Only a demon can raise an angel...

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:26.740
Flight of the Amazing Angel

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.810
Flight of the Amazing Angel

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.810
"Flight of the Amazing Angel"

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.680
Flight of the Amazing Angel

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:40.620
The perfect Angel's Maneuver you're shooting
for is just like I told you yesterday.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.660
Have you burned the image into your mind?

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:44.530
Yes.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:48.160
Then do right-leg-only squats on that log.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.130
But do it without making the water ripple.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.070
If you can't do this, there's no point in going on.

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.870
I understand.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.180
When you can do it on either leg, come get me.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.920
Right!

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:19.190
Come on, let's all do what we need to do.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.500
Okay.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.990
I'll stay with Sora a little longer.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.630
All right, take care of her.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:34.440
This is going to take a long time, isn't it?

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.580
Again...

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.270
Do you believe that Sora will become
a true Kaleido Star?

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.300
To be honest, I can't tell yet.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.940
I can't tell, but I'm thinking
I'll try betting this on Sora.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.880
You believe in this that much,

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:11.750
but you didn't take any steps
when she went back to Japan?

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.950
If she hadn't come back,

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.890
it would have meant that was the
highest level player she could be.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:20.120
Other than invite Leon here,
I haven't done anything.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:23.320
If I had to say, I suppose all
I did was terminate her contract...

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:29.060
If Sora can really become a true Kaleido Star,
no matter how many detours she takes,

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:31.730
I'm sure she'll find her own path.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.400
And in fact, she did come back.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.610
Or rather, it's almost as if the stage is in love
with her and doesn't want to let her go.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.840
In love?

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:46.210
In that case, perhaps what I'm feeling
right now is jealousy.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.740
Kalos, I have one proposal.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.130
I want some move...

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:01.490
I want a new move to compete
with the Angel's Maneuver.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.750
Softly...

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.790
Aw, it's rippling!

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.050
No good...

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.230
I wonder if I can really do this...

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:34.820
Sora!

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.530
Huh?

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.500
You've stopped already, Sora?

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.300
Sora?

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:44.360
I-l-I g-g-got a l-l-little c-c-cold...

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.510
Thanks for the food!

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.150
It's warming me up!

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.220
You can't push yourself too hard!

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.650
I know...

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:01.420
It's a good thing Marion was with you.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.690
Sora!

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.420
Hey, will you take a look at this?

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:06.930
Mia! Did you get an idea?

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:11.900
Yep! I've talked about it with Miss Cathy
too, and I think it might be good,

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.000
but I wonder what you'll think, Sora.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.560
The rest of you shout out your
opinions too, okay?

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.170
How cute!

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.750
Aren't they just?

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:28.980
Now, there are a lot of different
interpretations of Swan Lake,

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:32.390
but the most orthodox one is that even
though they defeat the demon,

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:38.060
Odette and Prince Siegfried both die
and they're joined together in Heaven.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.130
What about Odile, the demon princess?

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:42.760
That's right! That's the mystery!

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:46.200
After she's tricked the prince,
she disappears from the story!

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.300
Odile loved the prince too, right?

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.730
Can't there be a story where
Odile gets to be happy too?

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.740
I thought you'd say that.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.010
And so I tried thinking of Odile

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:01.180
as another personality that lives inside Odette.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:04.250
Odette is the loving heart
that cares for the prince,

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.720
and Odile is the hate that heart, which wanted
a monopoly on love, gave birth to.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:12.090
Even though they're in conflict,
what they seek is the same.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.560
Odette realizes that hate too is a form of love,

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:20.160
and her love grows to be so great
that it encompasses everything.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.470
Hate is love too...

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:26.870
Odette accepts Odile's hate,
and she turns into love itself.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:29.810
I want to try expressing that Odette
with the Angel's Maneuver!

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.750
A happy ending!

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:33.010
Not bad!

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.850
Truly an angel.

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:36.320
Really?

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.580
Sora?

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.760
Sora, is something wrong with it?

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:46.730
Oh, no, I think it's good! It's really great!

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:50.160
I was wondering if I could really
play such a great angel.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.270
There's nothing to fear on that score!

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:56.030
Because I've written it all tailored to
your normal personality, Sora!

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:56.700
Okay.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:57.410
Yay!

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:57.410
Okay.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:09:00.200
All right, I'm starting to get fired up!

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:04.550
The angel Mia envisions...

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:09.610
So she accepts her hatred, and becomes a
great love that encompasses everything, huh?

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.050
That might be something
a true star needs to do too.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:20.900
But I crumbled under the atmosphere of
the Circus Festival and ran away.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.660
Can I become that kind of angel?

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:28.330
An angel, huh?

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:42.720
We've decided that Kaleido Stage's first show
after its reopening will be Swan Lake.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.760
The lead, Sora Naegino, will present to you
the maneuver of a true Kaleido Star.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:49.890
I hear the Angel's Maneuver will be used?

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:53.590
Sora Naegino failed in the
Circus Festival, didn't she?

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.730
I have enough confidence in her
to open the show.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.270
She hasn't mastered it yet, has she?

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:03.330
Mr. Leon, are you satisfied with
Sora Naegino as a partner?

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:11.330
Of course I am.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.020
It's rippling...

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:31.930
It's no good.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.970
The rippling of the water
is a wavering of the heart.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:40.740
She cannot become a true star while
she still harbors uncertainty.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.740
The angel Mia envisioned for me...

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:49.150
An angel who accepts even hatred.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:52.350
She accepts battles, hatred, and everything else.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:53.890
If I can't do that,

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:59.450
maybe I can't become a true Kaleido Star
even if I DO perfect the Angel's Maneuver.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:04.890
The reality is, you won against me
and got the lead role.

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:08.500
After all, when all's said and done,
I'm competing with May.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:10.200
What do you mean, you don't want to battle?!

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.570
You're just running away from the
competition, that's all!

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:18.330
You should think carefully about how
much your attitude just now hurt May.

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:24.280
It's impossible to become a star without
being hated or begrudged by anybody.

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:30.220
If I admit that a stage without hatred or fighting
is a dream that will never be realized,

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:32.130
I won't have to agonize like this.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:35.390
So you're thinking that the best thing
is for you to have it easy?

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:40.230
But you shouldn't forget the feelings of the
people who are watching, now should you?

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:42.500
I know that, but...

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:43.500
Then...

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:47.940
instead of a sports bra, one with more frills or
something would be more pleasing to look at...

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:49.980
What are you doing?!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.710
What do you mean, "what"?

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:55.120
I was just trying to unpack your boxes for you!

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:56.080
Out of goodwill!

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:57.490
Thanks, but no thanks.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.120
I see...

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:02.920
I thought you were giving me advice for once.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.530
Yes, advice about your underwear...

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.160
Thanks, but no thanks!

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.560
If you've become uncertain,

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:11.290
it's also important to try taking a break
from practice to change your mood.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:12.700
But...

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:15.860
Are you confident you can do it just
by throwing yourself into it headlong?

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:17.570
Well...

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.040
Then your chances are the same either way.

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:21.940
Yeah, you're right.

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:25.480
Maybe I'll try going to Cape Mary Park;
I haven't been there in ages.

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:28.350
While you're at it, it would be great
if you'd buy some panties with ruffles.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.750
I won't!

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.250
No uncertainty there, huh...

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:06.850
I guess even people who look happy sometimes
fight and hate while I'm not there to see them.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.490
I should have kept practicing after all.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:11.480
This isn't making me feel even a bit better...

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:20.630
Angels...

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:32.040
It's no good, I don't get it.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:35.740
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:40.110
Um, I didn't notice you there...

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:42.920
Is he okay?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.460
Yes, he's not hurt.

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:48.660
Good boy. You handled that so well, Love.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.320
Good dog.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.500
Thank goodness. I'm sorry!

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.270
It looks like that wasn't intentional, then.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.170
Of course not!

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:03.580
Some people do intentionally step on his feet or
his tail when they realize he's a seeing-eye dog.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:04.810
Intentionally?

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.010
Yes.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:10.650
Seeing-eye dogs are trained not to bark while
they're working, no matter what happens.

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:13.050
So they step on him to check and see if he will.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.690
I'm Donna Walker, his trainer.

00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:17.330
This boy's name is Love.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:19.360
He's training to be a seeing-eye dog.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:21.800
I'm Sora Naegino.

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:24.570
I'm sorry, Love. It must've hurt, huh?

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:26.630
Miss Sora Naegino?

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:29.670
Not the one that's slated for the
lead role in Swan Lake?

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.110
Um, yes!

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:32.070
Skipping practice?

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.640
Kalos contacted me,

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:39.410
saying he by all means wanted me to come
and watch a true star be born.

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:43.680
But skipping is bad, isn't that right, Love?

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:47.120
For the boss to contact her directly...
Who is she?

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.620
But I feel like I've seen her somewhere before...

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:02.940
Well, we're still in the middle of training.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:05.200
Go straight, Love!

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:09.740
You're the Donna Walker who played Alice?!

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:10.580
Yes.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.480
I'm a huge fan of yours!

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:15.920
Oh, that's right, could you please sign my shirt?!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:22.550
Yay! Thank you so much!

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.230
I'm sorry I ended up following you all
the way to your training ground.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:30.930
That's okay, it's kind of a nice feeling
thinking that you're my fan.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:34.240
I'm not the only one! Miss Layla is too!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:39.700
But you'd already quit when Miss Layla
joined the troupe, huh?

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:44.940
Yes. I couldn't bear to stand
on the stage anymore.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:51.020
The pain of having to climb to the top
even if it meant stepping on someone

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:54.490
and the pressure of thinking someone
might overtake me someday.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:58.650
It seemed to me like everyone
around me had demons' hearts.

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:02.620
So one day, I ran away.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:08.590
I couldn't work up the desire
to be on stage again.

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:14.440
But... But your shows were fun,
and they sparkled.

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:16.410
They were really great!

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:23.620
I believe that Alice if nothing else
was bathed in smiles onstage and off!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.980
That you couldn't have had hatred or fighting...

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:33.260
Normally I'd tell you you were right,
but you're a stage performer.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.400
So I'll tell you the truth.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.670
Then you mean...

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:40.900
Yes. The reason I couldn't endure any
longer was because

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:44.810
I felt like I was deceiving audience
members like you, Sora.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.470
Love, up!

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:49.880
But I was mistaken in my thinking.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:52.570
These dogs taught me that.

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:55.450
They're angels.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:57.180
Angels?

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:00.240
Yep, slightly mischievous angels.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:04.860
Excuse me, what does it mean that
the dogs are angels?

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.590
Please tell me!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.070
It might be scary at first.

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:12.900
Okay.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.540
All right, let's go.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.330
Love, up!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.270
Go straight!

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:21.910
Don't brace against him.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:22.710
Right!

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:27.350
So fast...

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.120
Wait, that's too fast!

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.380
Love, stop!

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:32.320
Were you scared?

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.620
Yeah.

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:36.960
But that was slower than a normal walking pace.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.460
Really?!

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:43.060
Love felt your unease through the
harness and walked slowly for you.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:46.030
Now, trust Love and try it again.

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:47.000
Okay.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.530
Love, go!

00:17:56.510 --> 00:18:00.210
Huh? This might be going well.
It might! It might!

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.450
Huh? Wait, where are you going, Love?

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:04.350
That's not the right way...

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:06.650
Ow!

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:09.060
He tried to avoid an obstacle.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.360
Follow where Love leads you.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.950
Right.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:17.360
Huh?

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:18.630
Go!

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.120
What's wrong? Love, go!

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:23.800
Sora, take off your mask.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.910
If this were a real street,
you could have been hit by a car.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.520
Good dog, Love. Good boy.

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:36.180
You praise him too, Sora.

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:38.620
Good boy, Love! Thanks!

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:41.380
Good dog! Very good!

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:46.760
Was that hard?

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:47.900
Yes.

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:50.530
They do all kinds of training like this.

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:54.000
But only about one in three
become seeing-eye dogs.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.770
The others become normal pet dogs.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.610
Poor things...

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:02.980
Do you think the dogs are
being forced to train, Sora?

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.550
They're not?

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.980
Look closely. Do they look like they're suffering?

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.980
No, they look very happy.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:14.390
They know that if they follow instructions,
we'll be pleased.

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:19.220
The thing that makes them the happiest
is to please the people they're with.

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:21.330
Come! Love, come!

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:29.140
These creatures wish only to make
those around them happy.

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:32.590
That's why I think they're angels.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:37.510
Back then, I could only see
everyone's bad sides,

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:42.850
but after I met these guys, I realized
"Oh, it wasn't like that."

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:46.420
Everyone who stands on the stage
must have an angel's heart inside

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:51.590
that wants to give the audience a good time
and make everyone happy.

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:55.530
It's just that the feeling of
"l can do this better than her"

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:58.290
changes that angel heart to hatred.

00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:03.470
I'm sure you must have seen everyone's
angel hearts as you watched us on stage.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:08.110
Everyone's angel hearts...

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:09.580
Yes.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:12.710
Although I couldn't see them back then.

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:18.020
I see... During the Festival,
I couldn't see them either.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:21.890
When Mute and the others were talking about
their dreams with their friends,

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:23.420
their eyes weren't lying.

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:26.060
Everyone else had dreams too...

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:30.900
They all had angel hearts that wanted
to give the audience a good time...

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:35.360
And battles and hatred were the other side,
the result of that.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:39.070
"Hate is love too"... so THAT'S what it meant?

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:40.800
In that case...

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:45.430
You have a really serious look
on your face, so Love is worried.

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:48.450
Love, thanks!

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:51.590
Thanks to you, I think I can move forward again!

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:52.420
Sora.

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:53.320
Yes?

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:57.050
I've got high hopes for the birth of the true star.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.220
Yes! Thank you!

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:04.770
Maybe the Angel's Maneuver isn't a
maneuver to become an angel,

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:09.200
maybe it's a maneuver to wake up the
angel hearts inside everyone.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.640
No, I'm sure that's what it is!

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:14.840
I'll believe in the angel inside me.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.410
I'll believe in the angels inside everyone!

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:19.880
I'll believe in the Angel's Maneuver!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.280
Go for it, Sora!

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:24.820
Something's different than it was
up until yesterday, huh?

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:26.810
Maybe she's freed herself from her doubts.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:34.660
Won't doing it that slowly actually
cause more wavering?

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:37.720
No, the log isn't wavering.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.040
The water's not rippling!

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:11.870
She did it!

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:13.990
Right leg: success!

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:15.840
Amazing!

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:17.170
Impressive as always, Sora!

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:19.140
You did it!

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:19.140
She can really do it!

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:21.200
What kind of woman is she?!

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:27.350
It appears she's cleared the first stage.
Let's return home.

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:28.420
Yes, ma'am.

00:22:28.420 --> 00:22:29.810
Like, yes.

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:35.320
<i>All kinds of hard luck flocks your way
as if it's spurring you on</i>

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:35.320
<i>Sekasu you ni muragaru Hard luck</i>

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:38.550
<i>Swept away by it, time is over</i>

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:38.550
<i>Nagasarete Time is over</i>

00:22:39.560 --> 00:22:42.360
<i>Just as it was predicted, take it easy</i>

00:22:39.560 --> 00:22:42.360
<i>Yokoku douri Take it easy</i>

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:46.800
<i>I will get you out right away</i>

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:46.800
<i>Tsuredasu yo imasugu</i>

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:48.500
<i>Hurry up (Here we go)</i>

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:48.500
<i>Hurry up (here we go)</i>

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:50.470
<i>Forcibly only (Drive with the fastest speed)</i>

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:50.470
<i>Gouin only (saisoku drive)</i>

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:53.740
<i>The view I look down at every day is the best</i>

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:53.740
<i>Nichijo miorosu best view</i>

00:22:54.110 --> 00:22:56.180
<i>Sunset point (Favorite)</i>

00:22:54.110 --> 00:22:56.180
<i>Sunset point (favorite)</i>

00:22:56.180 --> 00:22:58.080
<i>Harbor light (Stormy night)</i>

00:22:56.180 --> 00:22:58.080
<i>Harbor light (stormy night)</i>

00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:01.880
<i>Escape for the sake of tomorrow</i>

00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:01.880
<i>Asuno tame ni escape</i>

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:08.560
<i>Even I don't have a vacation,
I've got an oasis</i>

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:08.560
<i>Bakansu nashi demo oashisu wa get</i>

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:14.980
<i>I'll turn off the cell phone
and charge my love</i>

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:14.980
<i>Keitai off tte ai o charge shite</i>

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:19.830
<i>Because some pain,
you can't soothe with just kindness</i>

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:19.830
<i>Yasashisa dake ja iyasenai itami mo aru kara</i>

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:23.700
<i>We are alone. We pass each other</i>

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:23.700
<i>We are alone. Surechigau</i>

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:25.110
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:25.110
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:30.370
<i>At the far end of regret,
I encounter my true heart</i>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:30.370
<i>Koukai no hate ni deau true heart</i>

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:37.750
<i>Whether I'm crying or laughing,
I will be with you</i>

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:37.750
<i>Naite mo waratte mo I'll be with U</i>

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:43.080
Next Kaleido Star: New Wings

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:47.060
I can't show the audience something fake!

00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:50.030
And so, Sora's intense training began.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.330
Why are you going that far? Stop this!

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:53.600
I won't stop!

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:56.040
I've come to get back my dream that
I entrusted to you,

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:59.470
or rather, the thing I left forgotten on the stage.

